// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// voxelbit.rc -- the icon Windows draws on the executable itself.
//
// (user 2026-09-21: "the icon now is just a regular .exe file. I want the
//  voxelbit icon logo".)
//
// THIS IS NOT THE WINDOW ICON. Two different things wear the same picture and
// they are set in two different ways:
//
//   * the WINDOW and TASKBAR icon is a runtime call -- see app_load.inl, which
//     overrides Falcor's nvidia.ico with game/logo.ico once the window exists.
//   * the icon EXPLORER draws on the file, and the one a Start Menu shortcut
//     inherits, is a Win32 resource compiled INTO the binary. Nothing at
//     runtime can supply it, which is why fixing the first left this one a
//     blank sheet of paper.
//
// ORDINAL 1, AND IT MATTERS. Windows shows the icon resource with the LOWEST
// ordinal as a file's icon, so this must be 1 and must be the only ICON in the
// binary -- Falcor adds none, so it is.
//
// THE PATH REACHES OUT OF THE ENGINE TREE and that is deliberate: game/ is the
// content root the engine already reads at runtime (build.bat passes --pines
// and --decor out of it), so the icon lives with the rest of the brand rather
// than being copied in and left to drift.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 ICON "../../../game/logo.ico"
